* Review of the Buddy PRs
** Functionally, these things changed:

   The branch adds a whole onboarding-companion ("buddy") feature plus supporting changes
   in the user, ingestion and GitHub modules (~27k added lines). There is no docs/tickets/
   or docs/plan/ directory in the repo, so the review could not be anchored against a
   ticket or planning brief.

*** The Buddy — persistent AI onboarding companion
    - One continuous, durable, tool-using AI conversation per user (separate from the
      existing multi-chat module).
    - API surface :: /api/v1/onboarding/me/buddy
      - GET /messages :: current visit's messages, oldest first.
      - GET /suggestions :: composer "chips" derived from the tools actually mounted for
        this hire.
      - POST /open/stream :: SSE opening greeting, streamed token by token.
      - POST /messages :: send a message; streams tool_use / token / citation /
        action_proposal / done / error events.
      - POST /actions :: confirm a buddy-proposed action (the only mutating path, always
        hire-confirmed).
    - Session behaviour
      - A memory note plus a cursor make the conversation durable across visits; the
        transcript is not replayed on reopen.
      - Opening twice without speaking replays the existing greeting; a broken stream
        persists whatever the hire already read (or a fallback welcome).
      - Agent loop :: the AI reasons, the backend executes tools it calls and feeds the
        results back, repeating up to 5 hops.
      - search_docs runs AI-side; retrieval is scoped to the hire's project ids.
      - The reply is emitted in word-sized chunks (paced emission, not true token streaming).
      - Compaction folds older turns into the memory note off the answering path
        (fire-and-forget, optimistic-locking guarded).
    - Read-only tools (mounted per hire) :: get_arrival_steps, get_my_metrics,
      get_my_competencies, get_competencies_to_assess, get_my_open_pull_requests (only when
      a GitHub login is set), get_suggested_tasks, search_canonical_answers, get_teammates,
      place_card (board tool, applies immediately, no confirmation).
    - Action tools (propose then hire-confirm) :: flag_to_pm, claim_task_zero,
      open_orientation, claim_goal, request_attestation, set_github_login, record_assessment.
    - Actions are re-scoped to the caller server-side at confirm time; handled failures
      return ok=false rather than an error.
    - Suggestion chips are a fixed catalog keyed to tool names; no action tools, no
      search_canonical_answers, and no place_card chips.

*** The hire's Board
    - Endpoints :: /api/v1/onboarding/me/board and /me/board/cards/...
    - A board is per user + project, created on first read, 404 when not a project member.
    - Baseline cards (auto-ensured on every read) :: PATH_TO_FIRST_CONTRIBUTION,
      ARRIVAL_STEPS (only when steps exist), OPEN_PULL_REQUESTS.
    - Mentor-placed cards (buddy via place_card) :: CURRENT_TASK, SUGGESTED_TASKS,
      COMPETENCY_PROGRESS, MEMORY_RECAP, DIAGRAM.
    - Hire-authored cards :: NOTE, LINK, CHECKLIST (several allowed; the mentor can never
      touch them). Endpoints to add, edit, reorder and dismiss.
    - Card content is read live (nothing stored except hire-authored cards and diagrams);
      DIAGRAM keeps a cached picture revalidated against a corpus fingerprint
      (GET /me/board/cards/{cardId}/diagram).
    - Dismissal is sticky (the row is kept as DISMISSED); the mentor cannot re-add a
      dismissed card.
    - On read, arrival steps and then the current task are pinned to the top; the hire's
      own order is preserved underneath.

*** Arrival steps
    - Authoring :: /api/v1/onboarding/arrival-steps
      - ADMIN/PM write, HR reads; scoped by optional projectId (company-wide vs project).
      - list, create, update, reorder, delete; the key is immutable.
      - GET /derivable :: the two system-checkable derivations (github-account,
        environment-ready).
    - Hire self-serve :: /api/v1/onboarding/me/arrival
      - List own steps (union of company-wide plus every project the hire belongs to).
      - POST /me/arrival/{key}/confirm :: settle a step with rigor DECLARED; idempotent;
        only self-confirmable steps.
      - POST /me/arrival/refresh :: re-check the observable steps.
    - Observation settles but never unsettles; github-account runs a GitHub existence
      check and records the verification verdict; environment-ready checks for any
      produced work.
    - Nothing anywhere is gated on arrival steps.

*** Starter-work pool
    - Endpoints :: /api/v1/onboarding/starter-work
      - POST /generate and POST /generate/stream (ADMIN/PM/HR) :: AI mining of the
        ingested corpus's open tracker issues into LIVE proposals; claimable immediately,
        reviewed=false.
      - POST / (ADMIN/PM) :: hand-author a task (born reviewed).
      - GET /candidates :: deterministic list of open corpus issues with pool state
        (AVAILABLE / IN_POOL / REMOVED) and hasAssignee.
      - POST /candidates/promote :: add a browsed issue (409 when already pooled, removed,
        or closed at its source).
      - GET /unreviewed, GET /pool, POST /{id}/review (lifts the ranking demotion,
        idempotent), POST /{id}/reject (sticky removal; mining never re-proposes).
      - GET /me/matches (USER) :: deterministic, self-explaining ranking via the matcher.
      - POST /me/goal and DELETE /me/goal :: claim/clear a goal (only LIVE tasks).
    - Matcher weights :: competency overlap 40, task type 20, repo familiarity 20, label
      familiarity 10, newcomer-safe-type bonus 8, unreviewed penalty -5, repository
      responsiveness penalty up to -15 (demotes, never hides).

*** Task 0
    - POST /starter-work/{proposalId}/task-zero (ADMIN/PM) :: flag a LIVE task as
      Task-0-eligible.
    - GET /me/task-zero (any role) :: auto-assigns on first read (no environment gate);
      noneAvailable and loopProven are ordinary states.
    - DELETE /me/task-zero :: undo the assignment (no-op when none).
    - Task 0 credits nothing (no competency write); completing it is a merged PR.

*** Task orientation
    - GET /me/orientation and POST /me/orientation/stream :: AI-assembled, step-segmented,
      cited packet for the current task, cached against a corpus fingerprint.
    - Cache rules :: unchanged serves the cache; skipped deletes it; a transport failure
      serves the cache; nothing is ever fabricated.
    - PUT /me/orientation and DELETE /me/orientation :: the hire pins or reverts their own
      task's orientation (fix in place).
    - GET / PUT / DELETE /orientation/tasks/{taskId} :: a PM authors or reverts a task's
      orientation.
    - Human packets are HUMAN-origin :: served verbatim, never re-assembled, never
      auto-deleted as stale.
    - Steps :: SET_UP, FIND_THE_CODE, MAKE_THE_CHANGE, CHECK_LOCALLY, OPEN_THE_PR.

*** Competency ledger and placement
    - GET /me/competencies (USER) :: the full durable ledger (level + ASSESSED / VERIFIED /
      DECLARED source).
    - Placement happens via the buddy's record_assessment action.
    - The placement service adopts the user's declared skills into the ledger as DECLARED
      (name-matched, lazily, once), returns unplaced competencies (max 12) ordered by
      whether the live pool needs them, and writes monotonically.
    - A VERIFIED row is never overwritten (accepted work outranks chat placement).

*** Ramp and autonomy
    - Stages :: TASK_ZERO -> TASK_ONE -> TASK_TWO_PLUS -> AUTONOMOUS, derived on read
      from accepted contributions.
    - Accepting work lazily credits the claimed goal's competencies at their target level
      as VERIFIED (monotonic).
    - Autonomy :: a contribution accepted with zero rework and zero human escalation
      during its window; recorded once, dated at acceptance rather than at notice time.

*** Contributions and evidence providers
    - A contribution is the four moments (opened / first-response / accepted / returned)
      unified across three sources; rigor is never blended.
    - PULL_REQUEST :: OBSERVED; merged = accepted, open = in flight, closed-unmerged =
      abandoned.
    - TRACKED_ISSUE :: OBSERVED; from ingested issues assigned to the hire's display
      name; acceptance only when somebody else moved it to Done; no abandoned state.
    - ATTESTATION :: ATTESTED; from the attestation table.

*** Attestations
    - Endpoints :: POST /me/attestations, GET /me/attestations, GET /attestations/pending,
      POST /attestations/{id}/accept, POST /attestations/{id}/send-back,
      POST /me/attestations/{id}/withdraw.
    - Rules :: attester cannot be the hire (400), both parties must be on the project
      (404/400), only the named attester may answer (403), send-back requires a reason
      (400) and increments returnedCount, withdraw rejects already-accepted work (409).

*** Knowledge base and escalations
    - Hire :: POST /me/knowledge-requests, GET /me/knowledge-requests.
    - PM/HR/ADMIN :: GET /knowledge-requests (inbox), POST /knowledge-requests/{id}/answer,
      POST /knowledge-requests/{id}/dismiss, GET /canonical-answers,
      PUT /canonical-answers/{id}.
    - Answering mints a durable canonical answer and closes the request against it; the
      buddy searches canonical answers with a simple token-overlap match (max 3).

*** Metrics and attention
    - Endpoints :: /api/v1/onboarding/metrics
      - GET /me :: the hire's own timeline, project-scoped.
      - GET /projects/{projectId} :: aggregates (median/p90 time-to-first-response, median
        time-to-first-accepted-contribution, stalls, unattributable members,
        waiting-on-response).
      - GET /projects/{projectId}/users/{userId} :: one hire's timeline.
      - GET /projects/{projectId}/attention :: who needs a human, BLOCKED before DRIFTING.
    - Stall thresholds :: 48h without a first response; 14 days quiet since joining or
      claiming a task.

*** GitHub history prior and consent
    - Consent-gated derivation of a hire's prior work (counts per type: / repo: / label:
      bucket) from already-ingested artifacts.
    - Granting consent computes the prior immediately; revoking deletes the row.
    - Placements already earned from the prior stay.

*** User module changes
    - New user fields :: githubLogin, githubLoginSource (SELF_DECLARED / PM_CONFIRMED),
      githubLoginVerification (VERIFIED / NOT_FOUND), githubLoginVerifiedAt,
      jiraDisplayName, githubSeedingConsentAt, lastSeenAt.
    - PatchMeRequest and PatchUserRequest gain optional githubLogin and jiraDisplayName;
      the PM path records PM_CONFIRMED.
    - GitHub login rules (single writer) :: trim/lowercase, GitHub username regex (400),
      uniqueness (409), blank clears, changing the login clears the verification verdict.
    - Jira display name rules (single writer) :: whitespace collapse, uniqueness (409),
      blank clears, no syntax rule, not case-folded.
    - getMe now derives and syncs local roles from JWT realm roles (Keycloak authoritative)
      instead of always USER.
    - User deletion publishes a UserDeletedEvent; the onboarding listener erases the
      user's buddy session and messages, boards and cards, ledger, arrival states, goals,
      Task 0, autonomy milestone, their own attestations, knowledge requests and history
      prior. Attestations they granted, and the shared catalog/pool/answers, are kept.
    - Session detection :: a filter stamps lastSeenAt on authenticated requests and
      publishes a UserSessionStartedEvent after an idle gap (sprintstart.session.idle-threshold,
      default PT4H).
    - Project roles refactor :: roles now hang off the project assignment/user. New
      endpoints :: GET/POST/DELETE /projects/{projectId}/users/{userId}/project-roles,
      POST /users/{userId}/project-roles, DELETE /users/{userId}/project-roles/{roleId}.
      Role deletion detaches holders first. ProjectUserResponse gains projectRoleRefs.
      ProjectUserAssignment gains assignedAt (join time).
    - ProjectMembershipApi (new) :: getProjectMembers (displayName, githubLogin,
      jiraDisplayName, joinedAt).
    - UserApi additions :: getGithubLoginByUserId, getDeclaredSkills, getGithubSeedingContext,
      setGithubSeedingConsent, setGithubLogin, recordGithubLoginVerification; UserDto gains
      skills. The user-search role filter now traverses assignments.

*** Ingestion changes
    - Artifact gains columns :: state, hasAssignee, authorLogin, mergedAtSource,
      firstResponseAtSource, changesRequestedCount, labels; createdAtSource/updatedAtSource
      are now persisted.
    - GitHub ingestion :: issues refresh state/labels unconditionally (hash gates only
      title/body); pull requests overwrite title/body/state/merge/first-response/
      changes-requested unconditionally; authorLogin is backfilled when null.
    - Jira ingestion :: issues now set state (Done category -> CLOSED, else OPEN) and
      hasAssignee (definite true/false), refreshed unconditionally.
    - The GitHub mapper now derives mergedAtSource, firstResponseAtSource (earliest
      non-self review or comment) and changesRequestedCount (non-self CHANGES_REQUESTED
      reviews); issues carry authorLogin/state/labels.
    - AssignedIssueReader (new) derives openedAt / firstResponseAt / acceptedAt /
      returnedCount for an assigned Jira issue from its changelog.
    - ArtifactIngestionApi additions :: getAuthoredWork, getAuthoredPullRequests,
      getAssignedIssues, getTaskSource, getOpenIssues, getIssue, getRepositoryResponsiveness,
      findArtifactById. The AI ingest request/mapper now carry state, hasAssignee, labels.
    - Artifact metadata deserialization now uses Jackson DEDUCTION and registers the Jira
      wrapper (fixes reading Jira metadata back).

*** GitHub connector changes
    - userExists(login) :: three-valued (true/false/null), unauthenticated; only a 404
      means "no such account".
    - fetchPullRequest (deep single-PR GraphQL) and fetchPullRequestFiles (REST diffs,
      capped at 100 files).
    - getPullRequestEvidence (new) :: assembles PR evidence with a character budget
      (12k total / 4k per file) and omittedFileCount.
    - The GraphQL PR model gains statusCheckRollup, files and commits; reviews gain
      submittedAt; new query 100-pullrequests-deep.graphql.

*** Config and shared
    - SecurityConfig installs the session-boundary filter after the bearer filter (via an
      optional ObjectProvider).
    - application.yaml adds sprintstart.session.idle-threshold (default PT4H).
    - StreamExecution, SyncExecution, WebClient, KnowledgeGap and KnowledgeGapsController
      are comment/KDoc-only changes (no functional change). DevUserSeeder is comment-only.

*** Flags for the review
    - No ticket, plan or ADR documents exist under docs/, so the ticket/plan/ADR
      comparison cannot be performed.
    - The working tree also contains an unrelated package-info.java whitespace edit and
      untracked Eclipse files (.classpath, .project, .settings/), likely not part of the
      PR's intent.
